Using $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ data, a precise determination of the $|V_{ts}|$ factor from a fit is sought, with the aim to reach an error of less than 0.01. To achieve this level of precision, it is essential to assess the impact of QCD uncertainties on the $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ decay rate. This paper examines the theoretical descriptions of the decay rate in the vicinity of the charm quark mass and identifies potential sources of discrepancy among them. Furthermore, this study investigates the QCD corrections to the decay rate and related hadronic form factors, with the ultimate goal of selecting the suitable theoretical framework to ensure reliable predictions for the $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ decay rate within the relevant kinematic region.
